From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:55:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegation): a resumed Claude subagent follows its chat
 onto an API-key provider

0147 keeps a resumed subagent on the provider it ran on, so a subagent recorded on claude-pool kept billing the pool after the user moved the chat to an Anthropic API-key provider. A recorded claude-pool route now moves to the chat's API-key provider when the chat runs on one now. A resume the chat asks for (action=resume) moves the route against the live chat and records that answer; a unit a gateway restart carried asks the chat's row for what its last turn ran on, since the record holds the answer from the spawn. A route on any other provider, a route that carried a credential (reask) and a chat on the pool keep what they had.
